    ` "н",
    `!"n, bc, r, c",
    `""`$ н  (en) is a consonant that does not have a direct equivalent in the `& alphabet  In Russian  it is pronounced like the `&  n   but with a slightly softer sound  It appears frequently in Russian words and plays a significant role in shaping the pronunciation of syllables  For example  the word for  new  in Russian is  новый  (novyi)  where the  н  sound is found twice  In general  it s important for `& speakers to learn how to recognize and produce this sound correctly when studying or speaking Russian ",
