    ` "были",
    `!"were",
    `""`$ были  (in the past participle form  были себя  or  былися   which can be translated as  were  in `&) is closest to the meaning of  contained  or  included  when used with a spatial sense  However  it s important to note that its usage may vary depending on context and grammatical construction  In a sentence like  Этот город был в этой стране несколько веков назад  и там была такой же жизнь   (This city was in this country several centuries ago  and there was such life) it can imply the city existed or was located within the country during that time  But always remember that the best way to understand a language is through practice  exposure  and immersion ",
