    ` "ещё",
    `!"one, two",
    `""`$ ещё  (yet  still  or more) is a versatile word that can be used in various contexts  For `& speakers  it could be compared to  yet    still   or  more  depending on the sentence s structure and context:\n\n1   Yet  when used as an adverb (as in  I will finish this work yet  )  meaning until now  up to a particular time  or possibly in the future \n2   Still  when used as an adverb (as in  It is still raining  )  meaning continuing at the present moment  persisting  or continuing despite something else having happened \n3   More  when used as a noun or adjective (as in  I want ещё кофе   or  I want more coffee  )  In this context  it means additional  further  or another \n\nIt s important to note that the usage and connotations of  ещё  can vary slightly depending on the sentence structure and intonation  Understanding the nuances will come with practice and exposure to more Russian conversations ",
