  {
    ` "й",
    `!"nd",
    `"" In the Russian alphabet  the letter  й  (pronounced as  i  in `& but without the  e ) is a vowel  It s unique because it s always followed by another vowel and has no equivalent in the `& language  This combination of a  й  followed immediately by a vowel often softens the sound of the following consonant  For example  in the word  дом  (house)  without the  й   it would be pronounced as  dom   But with the  й  before the  о   it s pronounced as  dyom  ",
