    ` "з",
    `!"r, e, rp, gd",
    `"" The Russian letter  з  is pronounced like the `& letter  z   It represents a voiced alveolar sibilant consonant in the Russian alphabet  Its phonetic value is similar to the  s  sound in words like  zebra  or  azure   but it s more palatalized  meaning that the back of the tongue is slightly raised towards the hard palate during articulation  This results in a sound that may seem closer to an  sh  or  zh  sound for some `& speakers  However  the exact pronunciation may require practice to master due to differences in the muscular movements involved and the nuances of Russian phonetics ",
