    `!"dmitry, dmitri",
    `#"0.0001176412",
    `""The Russian name Дмитрий`(\"Dmitri\" in `&. This is a popular male name of Greek origin, which means \"belonging to the gods.\"\n\nIf you're learning Russian, it might be helpful to remember that the letter \"i\" in Dmitriy sounds like the \"ee\" sound in \"feet,\" and the ending \"-iy\" represents a diminutive form. So, if someone has the surname Dmitriev (Дмитриев), they could informally be called Dmitriyevich (Дмиtriевич) or just Dima (Дима)."
