    `""`$ слово  (slovo) can be translated as  word  in `&  It is a noun that refers to a unit of language  a spoken or written symbol string that conveys a particular meaning  In Russian grammar  slovo is the basis for forming many other words and phrases  For example  an adjective (прилагательное) is formed by adding -ый (-y) at the end of a noun  making  слово  become  словянский  which means Slavic  or by adding -ого at the end to make it a masculine singular noun  like  слова  (words)  It can also be used in plural form (слова) when referring to multiple words ",
