  },
  {
    ` "предшественник",
    `!"predecessor",
    `""`$ предшественник  (predshestvénnik)`( forerunner  or  predecessor  in `&  It is used to denote someone who comes before another  often in a chronological sense  such as a person who held an office or position before another  or someone whose ideas paved the way for subsequent developments ",
    `#"8.32536e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "отношении",
    `!"case, whereas, sensitive",
    `""`$ отношении  (otnoshenii) can be translated as  relation    regard   or  standing   It s a plural noun in the instrumental case  which often indicates the instrument  agency  or means by which something is done  In other words  when referring to a specific relationship or attitude  it would typically take the nominative or accusative cases:  отношения  (otnosheniia) for the nominative (the subject of the sentence)  and  отношения  (otnosheniiia) for the accusative (the direct object)  For example   Отношения между странами в наше время сложны  means  Relations between countries nowadays are complicated   or  Я хочу улучшить отношения с ним  can be translated as  I want to improve my relations with him  ",
    `#"8.32024e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "лица",
    `!"persons, person",
    `""`$ лица  (licas)`( faces  in `&  It is used to refer to multiple faces or countable instances of a face  like people s faces or facial expressions  For example  you might say   Мне на лице – это счастье  ( Mne na licu - eto schast e )  which means  I am smiling because I am happy  ",
    `#"8.3184e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "относительно",
    `!"relatively, relative",
