    ` "ил",
    `!"mig, isbn, aero, bac",
    `""`$ ил  (pronounced  il ) is a conjunction that has several functions in the language  but it s most commonly used to introduce conditions or hypothetical situations  For example  in the sentence  Если я иду ил ты спишь  то кто будет разводить меня?  (If I go and you sleep  who will wake me up?)   ил  connects the conditional clause  если я иду  (if I go) with the consequence clause  то кто будет разводить меня?  (who will wake me up?)  It s important to note that the use of  ил  in this context can be replaced with  если бы   which is more commonly used in standard Russian  but  ил  is still a valid and frequently used option ",
