    ` "эль",
    `!"el",
    `""`$ эль  (pronounced as  el ) is not a common or widely used word in everyday Russian conversation  It is actually an archaic or historical term with multiple meanings:\n\n1  In Old Slavic mythology   Ел  or  El  was the name of a supreme deity  akin to the European pagan god of thunder and lightning \n\n2  In some regions  particularly Siberia   эль  can refer to shamans who practiced in ancient times  They were believed to communicate with spirits and guide people \n\n3  In more recent history   эль  can also mean a type of needle used for sewing or embroidery  specifically a long  slender  straight pin with a round eye \n\nSo  the word  эль  has a rich cultural and historical context in Russian  but it is not frequently encountered in contemporary usage ",
    `#"6.61049e-05"
  },
