    ` "бывший",
    `!"former",
    `""`$ бывший  (pronounced [bɨˈvizɪ] in standard Russian)`( former  or  ex-  when used before a noun  as in  бывший президент  ( ex-president ) \n\nHowever  the word you provided   и являвшимся  (pronounced [i ɪ konˈtavnəfʲɪm sə])  is not a standard Russian phrase  It seems to be a combination of  бывший  and the reflexive verb  и быть  (or  и являться )  which means  to be  or  to be (someone)   The correct way to use it in a sentence would be something like:  Он был президентом  а сейчас он является адвокатом  ( He was a president  and now he is an attorney ) \n\nThis construction of combining  быть  with the perfective aspect (бы-/стал/стала/стало) is used to describe someone s past role or position  as in this example  In `&  you could say  He was a president  now he is an attorney  ",
