    `!"red",
    `"" The Russian term  красноармейskim  (transliterated as  krasnoarmeyskim ) is an adjective derived from the noun  Красная Армия  (Krasnaya Armia)  which means  Red Army   It refers to anything related to  or originating from  the Red Army  In a broader sense  it could be used to describe things that have a Soviet military or socialist connotation  However  its usage and meaning may vary based on historical context and regional differences in Russia ",
    `#"5.98671e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "би",
    `!"bbc, radio, pbs, tay",
    `""`$ би  (pronounced  bih ) is a shortened form of the verb  бить  (to hit  beat or strike)  It s often used in expressions like  побить  (to beat) or  дать побить  (to give a beating)  In phrases like  подняться на битку  (to join a fight)  it can mean battle or fight  The short form  би  itself is usually not found as a standalone verb  but more commonly used as an interjection to express frustration or annoyance in colloquial Russian speech ",
    `#"5.98364e-05"
  },
  {
