    `""The Russian word \"являлся\" (which is masculine singular of \"являться\")`(\"was\" or \"had been\" in `& when referring to past continuous tense. For example: \"Я был в Москве вчера, я являлся инженером\" means \"I was in Moscow yesterday, I was an engineer.\" In present continuous, you would use \"являюсь\": \"Я являюсь инженером\" means \"I am an engineer.\""
