  {
    ` "иметь",
    `!"give, possess, hold, choose",
    `""`$ иметь  (pronounced as  ih-meht )`( to have  in `&  It is a verb and it s conjugated based on tense  number (singular or plural)  and person (first  second  or third)  For example  the present tense forms are:\n\n- есть (jest ) for first person singular and all other forms of the second and third persons in both numbers \n- имею (ih-mayu) for first person singular (informal) in present tense \n- have in `& is used for third person singular present tense  but in Russian  there s no difference between  he/she/it has  and  they have  in the present tense \n\nFor example:\nЯ есть студент (ya jest  student) - I am a student \nУ тебя есть книга? (u tebya jest  kniha?) - Do you have a book?\nОн имеет собаку  (On imeyet sobachku ) - He has a dog \nОни имеют два кота  (Oni imeyut dva kota ) - They have two cats ",
