    `!"rus",
    `""`$ русь  (transliterated as  Rus   or  Rus  ) is a historical term that originally referred to the early Eastern Slavic tribes living in the northeastern forests of Europe  predominantly within modern-day Russia and Ukraine  It was used to distinguish them from other neighboring tribes  The term eventually evolved and came to be associated with the emergence of Kievan Rus   a medieval state that laid the foundations for what would later become the Russian  Ukrainian  and Belarusian nations  In modern contexts  it is sometimes used symbolically in Russia to signify the cultural or spiritual unity of these three nations ",
