  {
    ` "любой",
    `!"any",
    `""`$ любой  (transliterated as  lyuboy ) is an adjective that can mean either  any  or  each   It s often used to indicate a nonspecific number of things  similar to the `& words  any  and  each   For example  in the sentence  Я смотрю любой фильм   which translates as  I watch any film   the word  любой  indicates that it doesn t matter which specific film is being watched \n\nHowever  it s important to note that there are subtle differences between  any  and  each  in `&  and these differences can sometimes be seen in the Russian language as well  For instance  if you say  Я смотрю каждый фильм   which means  I watch every film   it implies that all films will be watched  whereas saying  Я смотрю любой фильм  implies a lack of restriction on the choice of film being watched  as long as it s a film \n\nSo  while  любой  can generally be translated to  any  or  each   it carries more connotations of a nonspecific selection than the `& words do in certain contex",
