    ` "мер",
    `!"measures",
    `#"2.78099e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"мер\" can have multiple meanings depending on the context. Here are a few:\n\n1. A unit of measurement - equivalent to the meter in `& (used mainly in scientific or technical terms).\n2. Measure, as in a calculation or estimation - similar to 'measure' in `&.\n3. Municipality, district, or administrative division (more often used in plural form \"меры\") - similar to 'municipalities' or 'districts' in `&.\n4. In the idiom \"на меру\" it means suitable, appropriate, or just right - similar to 'to fit' or 'appropriate' in `&.\n\nHowever, as a learner of Russian, it would be helpful to learn the word within a sentence or context for better understanding. For example:\n\n1. \"Метр\" (meter) - Это единица измерения длины в метрах - This is a unit of measurement for length in meters.\n2. \"Мерять\" (to measure) - Мы должны выполнить меру для проверки дальности - We need to take a measurement to check the distance.\n3. \"Мера\" (municipality/administrative district) - В этом районе есть много домов - In this area, there are many houses.\n4. \"На меру\" (suitable or appropriate) - Это одежда на меру - This clothing fits well."
  },
