    ` "берега",
    `!"shores, shore",
    `#"2.56207e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"Берега\"`(\"Banks\" or \"Shores\" in `&. This could refer to the edges of a body of water (river or sea) where land meets water, or it could also refer metaphorically to financial institutions."
  },
  {
    ` "малые",
    `!"small",
    `""`$ малые  (malye) can be translated to  small  or  younger  in `&  depending on the context  It is an adjective and is used to describe something that is small in size or stature  or something that is younger compared to others  For example   малая речка  (malaya rechka) means a small river  and  малые дети  (malye deti) refers to young children  In plural form  it can also mean smaller versions of things  like  малые картинки  (malye karтинki)  which`(small pictures or drawings ",
    `#"2.56187e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "дмитрия",
    `!"dmitry, dmitri",
    `#"2.56105e-05",
    `""The Russian name Дмитрия`(\"Dmitry\" in `&. If you want to say \"the man named Dmitry\", it would be \"Дмитрий (Dmitriy) - это мужчина (dmitriy - eto muzhchina)\" in Russian."
  },
  {
    ` "римского",
    `!"roman, rome",
    `""`$ римского  (pronounced  rimskoyo ) is a masculine adjective that`( Roman  or  of Roman origin  in `&  It is derived from the noun  Рим  (Rim)  which means Rome  the capital city of Italy and one of the most important cities of ancient history due to its role in the Roman Empire  So  when you encounter  римского   it typically refers to something related to or originating from Rome ",
    `#"2.55982e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "ввиду",
    `!"due",
    `""`$ ввиду  (vvidu) can be translated as  for the sake of   or  due to   It is often used to express a reason or cause  For example  you might say  Я не могу пойти на вечеринку ввиду работы  (Ya ne mogu poiti na vecherinku vvidu raboty)  which means  I cannot go to the party because of work   It s similar in usage to `& phrases like  due to  or  for the sake of   but it can also be used more loosely  such as  Я ввиду всего этого не согласен  (Ya vvidu vsego togo ne soglashen)  which means  I m not agreeing with all of this  ",
    `#"2.55614e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "великих",
    `!"great, greatest",
    `""`$ великих  (VELIKIH) is a plural noun that is most commonly used to refer to  great  or  important  people  places  or things in a historical or cultural context  It is derived from the adjective  великий  (VELIKIY)  which means  great  or  large  ",
