    ` "иисуса",
    `!"jesus",
    `#"2.52153e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"Иисуса\"`(\"Jesus\" in `&. This is a name and it refers to Jesus Christ in Christianity. It's spelled with capital letters in Russian (ИИСУСА), but when used as a part of a sentence, it would be written as Иисус or Иисуса (depending on the context). Learning new languages can be a rewarding journey, and I hope this helps you along your path to learning Russian!"
  },
  {
    ` "принцесса",
    `!"princess",
    `""`$ принцесса  (princessa) is a feminine noun  meaning  princess  in `&  It s derived from the masculine form  князь  (knyaz)  which means  prince   These terms are used to describe members of royal families or high-ranking nobility ",
    `#"2.5203e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "учения",
    `!"teachings, doctrines",
    `#"2.51989e-05",
    `""Учение means \"training\" or \"study\" in `&. It's commonly used when referring to educational courses, military training, or practice sessions in sports or any skill-based activity."
  },
  {
    ` "основного",
    `!"replacement, main, substituted, substitutes",
    `""`$ основного  (osnovnogo) is the masculine singular accusative case of the adjective  основной  (osnovnoy)  which means  main    primary   or  most important   In a sentence  it could be used like this:  Мне нужен основное решение  (I need the main/most important decision) ",
    `#"2.51968e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "кого",
    `!"anybody, them, so, anyone",
    `""`$ кого  (koho) is a pronoun and is used as the direct object form of  кого-кого  (kogo-kogda)  which means  whom  in `&  In other words  it s used to ask or answer questions about the subject of the action in Russian sentences  For example: Кому пишет это письмо? (Komu pishet eto pit mo?)`( To whom is this letter being written?  and a possible response could be: Я ему пишу (Ya yemu pishu)  which means  I am writing it to him  ",
    `#"2.51866e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "знаком",
