    `#"2.51805e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "аллен",
    `!"barry, davis, allen, harmon",
    `#"2.51784e-05",
    `""In `&, the Russian word \"аллен\" (Allen) is a given name that originates from a surname of German or Scottish origin. It means 'hollow' in Old `& and 'foreigner' in Gaelic. However, without a specific context, it's difficult to provide a precise translation for the word Allen as it functions mainly as a personal name in Russian. If you come across \"Allen\" in another context, such as a book or a movie title, I would suggest looking up the appropriate definition for that context."
  },
  {
    ` "советское",
    `!"soviet, ussr",
    `"" sovhozy (plural  singular - sovkhoz) is a Russian term derived from  советское хозяйство  (Soviet agriculture)  which refers to large-scale collective farms that were established in the Soviet Union  These farms were state-owned and operated as self-contained entities  often including housing  schools  healthcare facilities  and even factories for the production of goods needed by the farm  The goal was to maximize agricultural output while promoting communal living  Sovhozy played a significant role in the Soviet Union s economy  particularly during the period of collectivization in the 1930s ",
    `#"2.51743e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "значительное",
    `!"significant",
    `""`$ значительное  (Znachitel noye) is an adjective that`( significant    substantial   or  important  in `&  It can be used to describe objects  actions  events  or people that are of considerable value or consequence ",
    `#"2.51579e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "одежды",
    `!"clothing",
    `""`$ одежды  (odëždy) is the plural form of the noun  одежда  (odëžd a)  which`( clothes  or  apparel  in `&  This term covers a wide range of items like shirts  pants  jackets  dresses  and more  The singular form  одежда  is less commonly used in everyday conversations compared to the plural form  одежды  ",
    `#"2.51559e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "идей",
