  },
  {
    ` "другу",
    `!"pair, mutual, together, pairs",
    `""`$ другу  (pronounced [drʊˈɡu])`( to friend  in `&  However  when used as a noun  it means  friend   It is the accusative and genitive singular form of the Russian noun  друг  (pronounced [ˈdrʊk])  So   Я другу пишу  (Ya drugu pisu)`( I write to a friend   In this sentence   другу  functions as the direct object ",
    `#"2.00956e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "рис",
    `!"rice",
    `""`$ рис  (pronounced as  ris )`( rice  in `&  It is a commonly used food item in many parts of the world  and it is also a staple ingredient in many traditional Russian dishes  Rice can be cooked and eaten on its own  or used as an ingredient in other dishes such as soups  casseroles  and salads  It s versatile  nutritious  and easily digestible  making it a popular choice for people of all ages ",
    `#"2.00936e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "мальта",
    `!"malta",
    `#"2.00895e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"мальта\"`(\"Malta\" in `&. It is a country in the Mediterranean Sea, south of Sicily, Italy. Knowing this can help you in your journey to learn the Russian language."
  },
  {
    ` "океане",
    `!"ocean",
    `""`$ океане  (okeane) is the plural form of  океан  (ocean)  In `&  both words represent more than one large expanse of salt water  This term originates from the Ancient Greek word  okeanos   meaning  sea-god   It s fascinating to note that many languages share a similar root for ocean  demonstrating the universality and significance of this immense natural feature in human cultures ",
    `#"2.00813e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "запрещены",
    `!"prohibited, forbidden, banned",
    `#"2.00792e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"запрещены\" is translated as \"forbidden\" in `&. This word is used to express that something is not allowed or prohibited. For example, if a sign says \"Запрещена фотографирование,\" it means \"Photography is forbidden.\""
  },
  {
    ` "хьюстон",
    `!"houston",
    `#"2.00731e-05",
    `""Houston in `& is \"Хьюстон\"."
  },
  {
    ` "участке",
    `!"crossing, depot, station",
    `""`$ участке  (pronounced [ʊˈxatskʲɪ])`( plot of land  or  allotment  in `&  It is commonly used in a rural context  such as referring to private plots of land assigned to individuals for farming purposes under the Soviet system ",
    `#"2.0067e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "проводить",
    `!"perform, participate",
    `""`$ проводить  (pronounced: pro-vot-id-t ) can be translated as  to conduct  or  to carry out   However  it is most commonly used to mean  to accompany someone until they leave a place   or more generally   to see someone off   For example  one might say  Я провожу вас до станции  (Ya provozhu vas do stantsii) which means  I ll see you off at the station   It is important to note that the verb has a reflexive form (проводить себя  provodit  sebya) which means  to leave  or  to depart  ",
    `#"2.00629e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "чин",
    `!"rank",
    `""`$ чин  (chin)`( rank    grade   or  degree  in `&  It is often used to refer to military  governmental  or clerical ranks and titles  For example  a police officer might have a higher or lower  чин  depending on their rank within the department ",
    `#"2.00629e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "культурный",
    `!"cultural",
    `""`$ культурный  (kul turnyj)`( cultural  or  cultured  in `&  It refers to something that is related to arts  learning  or refinement  suggesting a high level of education  sophistication  or good manners  However  it can also be used to describe an environment that promotes these qualities ",
    `#"2.00608e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "федеральных",
    `!"federal",
    `""`$ федеральных  (federal nyh) is the plural form of  федеральный  (federal nyj)  which`( federal  in `&  It refers to entities  such as institutions or regions  that are part of or under the jurisdiction of the federal government of a country  For example  federal entities could include different states within a federation like Russia or the United States ",
    `#"2.00506e-05"
