    `""In `&, the Russian word мужскую`(\"male\" or \"for males\"."
  },
  {
    ` "валюты",
    `!"currency, currencies",
    `#"2.00465e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"валюта\"`(\"currency\" in `&."
  },
  {
    ` "дэн",
    `!"jeremy, donnie, jen",
    `#"2.0028e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"дэн\" is translated to \"day\" in `&. It's one of the basic vocabulary words for someone learning Russian and can be used in many different contexts like \"good day,\" \"tomorrow,\" or \"yesterday.\""
  },
  {
    ` "сумма",
    `!"sum",
    `""`$ сумма  (summa) is commonly translated as  sum  or  total  in `&  It s used to denote the amount of money  numbers  or values being added together  For example  if you are calculating the cost of a shopping trip  you might say   Сумма моего счета составляет 100 рублей  (The sum of my bill is 100 rubles) ",
    `#"2.0024e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "волость",
    `!"voivodeship, administrative",
    `"" Волость (volost ) in Russian is a historical term that refers to a subdivision of a larger territory  often a district or county within a principality or grand duchy in medieval Rus   It was a self-governing administrative division with its own court and local officials  In modern usage  the term might be used less frequently but generally retains its historical connotations as a rural or provincial area ",
    `#"2.00117e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "химических",
    `!"chemical",
    `#"2.00096e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"химических\"`(\"chemical\" in `&. This is an adjective used to describe things related to chemistry or chemicals. Keep practicing and you'll be fluent in no time!"
  },
  {
    ` "адольф",
    `!"adolf",
    `#"2.00096e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"Адольф\"`(\"Adolf\" in `&."
  },
  {
    ` "посетил",
    `!"visited",
    `""`$ посетил  (posetil) is the Past Tense of the verb  посещать  (posechchat )  which means  to visit  or  to pay a visit   In `&  the past tense would be  visited  in most cases  However  it s essential to note that the Russian language often uses a different word order compared to `&  and the subject is usually dropped when it is clear from context  For example:  Я посетил музей  (Ya posetil muzey)`( I visited the museum  ",
    `#"2.00076e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "церковью",
    `!"church",
    `""Церковью (church) in Russian refers to a religious building where Christians  primarily Orthodox Christians  gather for worship and religious services  It can also be used metaphorically to describe the Christian church as a whole or a specific denomination within Christianity ",
    `#"2.00055e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "независимых",
    `!"independent",
    `""`$ независимых  (nezávisimyh) can be translated as  independents   It s commonly used to refer to individuals or groups who are not affiliated with any political  social  or economic institutions  or who operate independently of such institutions  For instance  an independent political party would be known as независимых политическая партия in Russian ",
    `#"2.00035e-05"
  },
  {
