    `#"1.98888e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "монако",
    `!"monaco",
    `#"1.98867e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"Монако\" is actually not a Russian word but refers to Monaco, which is a principality (small independent country) located on the French Riviera in Western Europe. In `&, Monaco is pronounced as [məˈnækoʊ] or [məˈnaːkoʊ]. If you're learning Russian, it would be helpful to learn how to say countries and cities in both languages! For example, \"Монако\" (Monaco)`(\"Монокко\" (Monakko) in Russian."
  },
  {
    ` "кинорежиссёр",
    `!"screenwriter",
    `""`$ кинорежиссёр  is a noun that`( cinema director  or simply  film director  in `&  It refers to someone who oversees the production of a movie  including creative aspects like scripting  storyboarding  and guiding actors  as well as practical elements such as camera placement  lighting  and editing  Notable Russian film directors include Andrei Tarkovsky  Sergei Eisenstein  and Alexander Sokurov ",
