    `""The Russian word \"киевской\"`(\"Kyivsky (of or relating to Kyiv)\" in `&. It is an adjective that describes something originating from or associated with the city of Kyiv (also spelled as Kiev), the capital of Ukraine.\n\nFor someone learning Russian, it's essential to learn how to form the adjectives derived from proper nouns - cities, countries, rivers, mountains, etc. In this case, you can create the adjective \"киевский\" by adding the suffix \"-ский\" (-ский, -ская, -ское) to the name of the city \"Киев\".\n\nHere are a few more examples:\n\n- Москва (Moscow) -> московский (Moscow-related)\n- Санкт-Петербург (Saint Petersburg) -> петербургский (Saint Petersburg-related)\n- Вологда (Volgda) -> вологодский (Volgda-related)\n- Новосибирск (Novosibirsk) -> новосибирский (Novosibirsk-related)"
