    `""The Russian word \"находилось\"`(\"was located\" or \"was found\" in `&. If you are trying to learn Russian, you can break this word down into simpler parts:\n\n- Находить (nachinit') means \"to find\" or \"to look for\".\n- -ся (-sya) is a reflexive pronoun that means \"oneself\" and helps create the passive voice in Russian.\n\nSo, \"находилось\" combines these two elements to mean \"was found\" or \"was located\", usually referring to an object or a person moving to a certain place. Keep practicing and you'll be speaking Russian fluently soon!"
  },
  {
    ` "отсутствуют",
    `!"lacks, absent",
    `""`$ отсутствуют  (otstushchut) is the third-person plural form of the verb  отсутствовать  (otstustovat )  which`( are absent  or  are missing  in `&  So  when you say  отсутствуют   it means that multiple people are not present or something is not available at a particular place or time ",
