    `""The Russian word \"Кристина\"`(\"Christina\" in `&. This name is of Greek origin and means \"follower of Christ.\""
  },
  {
    ` "золотого",
    `!"gold, golden",
    `""`$ золотого  (zolotoGO) is an adjective that means  golden   It is derived from the noun  золото  (zoloto)  which`( gold  in `&  When you attach  о-go  (o-go) to the end of a noun  it turns it into an adjective meaning  of  relating to  or having the quality of   So   золотого  means something made of gold  golden colored  or associated with gold ",
    `#"1.81502e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "цен",
    `!"prices",
    `""`$ цен  (pronounced  tsen ) can be translated into `& as  price    cost   or sometimes  value   It s important to note that depending on the context  the term could refer to either monetary price or inherent value  For example  when you go shopping  the cost of an item is its price; but if someone says  она имеет высокую ценность  (she has a high value)  it means she s very important or valuable in another sense ",
    `#"1.81502e-05"
