  {
    ` "мн",
    `!"ir, e, em",
    `""`$ мн  (mn) is not a common standalone word in the Russian language  It is actually a contraction of two definite articles   мы  (mı) meaning  we  (used with masculine or mixed nouns)  and  наш  (naš) meaning  our   When used together in written Russian to refer to something possessed by both the speaker and someone else  they contract into a single form  мн  which is pronounced as [mn]  For example   мы - наш = мн-корабль  `( our ship  in `& ",
