    `!"hours",
    `""Сутки is the Russian word for  day   It comes from the Old Slavonic root  dŭxъ  or  день   which also appears in other Slavic languages like Ukrainian  Bulgarian  Serbian  and Czech  In a 24-hour context  it usually refers to one full rotation of Earth on its axis  but can sometimes be used figuratively to denote a period of time longer than one day ",
