    `!"crime",
    `""`$ преступление  (prestuplenie)`( crime  in `& ",
    `#"1.35302e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "сет",
    `!"manu, staples, domino, osiris",
    `""`$ сет  (set) can have multiple meanings depending on the context  It is often translated as  set  in `&  but it also has other uses such as:\n\n1  A collection or series of things: For example  a set of rules or a set of numbers \n2  To arrange or put something in order: For example  to set the table \n3  In sports  it can refer to a volleyball term where players attempt to spike the ball over the net and into the opponent s court  This is written as  задача  (zadacha) when being given or  блок  (blok) when it involves blocking the opposing team s spike \n4  In the phrase  поставить на стойки  (postavit na stoyki)  it means to put someone in prison  as in `& \n5  As a noun   сет  can mean an outdoor or indoor tennis court ",
    `#"1.35302e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "германский",
    `!"german",
    `""`$ германский  (germanskii) is an adjective used to describe something or someone that is German  It comes from the Germanic language and has roots in the Old High German word  Werinisc   which means  from Germany   In a sentence  for example: Это германский книжный магазин (Eto germanskii knizhnyi magazin)`( This is a German bookstore  in `& ",
    `#"1.35281e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "демография",
    `!"demographic",
    `""`$ демография  (demografiya) is translated as  Demography  in `&  Demography is the statistical study of human population  including its size  density  location  distribution  and composition  as well as the changes that take place over time due to birth rates  death rates  migration  and other factors  The term demography comes from the Greek words demos (people) and graphein (writing)  reflecting its focus on quantifying human populations ",
    `#"1.35281e-05"
  },
  {
