  },
  {
    ` "крестьяне",
    `!"peasants",
    `""`$ крестьяне  (krest yane)`( peasants  in `&  It refers to rural inhabitants who work on the land and are not noble  urban  or of another specialized social rank  In historical contexts  it can be used to describe a large segment of the Russian population during various periods of feudalism and serfdom ",
    `#"1.35097e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "явлений",
    `!"phenomena",
    `#"1.35097e-05",
    `""In `&, \"явлений\" (yavleniya)`(\"phenomena\". This noun refers to something that is visible or observable, especially a natural or scientific event or occurrence."
  },
  {
    ` "императорский",
    `!"imperial",
    `""`$ императорский  (imperorstkiy)`( imperial  or  relating to an emperor   It is often used in historical contexts  such as referring to the Imperial Family of Russia or Imperial Palace  In modern times it can be found in names of certain institutions that were once part of the Russian Empire  like the Imperial Ballet or the Imperial Academy of Sciences ",
