    `#"1.35077e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "детские",
    `!"children",
    `""`$ детские  (detskie) is an adjective that refers to something related to children or childhood  It s derived from the noun  дети  (deti)  which means  children   So  a toy box could be called  детский ящик  (detsky yashchik)  and a playground could be  детская площадка  (detskaya ploshchadka) in Russian ",
    `#"1.35056e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "даль",
    `!"liv, sig, med, il",
    `""`$ даль  (pronounced  dal )`( distance  or  far away  in `&  It can be used as an adverb  noun  or adjective depending on the context  For example:\n\n- Я уеду в дальний край страны (I am going to a distant part of the country)\n- Этот объект находится на большой дали (This object is far away)",
    `#"1.35036e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "одноимённой",
    `!"eponymous",
    `#"1.35036e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"одноимённой\"`(\"having the same name\" in `&. It is an adjective and is used to describe objects or concepts that share the same name. For example, \"одноимённые улицы\" means \"streets with the same name\"."
  },
  {
    ` "диалог",
    `!"dialogue",
    `""`$ диалог  (diálog) translates directly to  dialogue  in `&  It refers to a conversation or discussion between two or more people  often used in a formal context such as a debate or negotiation  It can also be used more broadly to describe any exchange of ideas or opinions between individuals or groups ",
    `#"1.35015e-05"
  },
  {
