  },
  {
    ` "единственная",
    `!"sole, only",
    `""`$ единственная  (yedinestvennaya)`( unique  or  only one of its kind  in `&  It is used to describe something that has no equal  is special  or is the only example of its kind ",
    `#"1.34995e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "названиям",
    `!"names",
    `""`$ названиям  (nazvaniyam) is a dative plural noun  and its literal translation into `& would be  to the names  or  in the names   It s used when referring to multiple names in a context such as addressing a group of individuals with different names  However  it s important to note that this word can have more nuanced meanings depending on the context  just like any other language ",
    `#"1.34995e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "грамматика",
    `!"grammar, phonology",
    `""`$ грамматика  (grammatika) translates directly to  grammar  in `&  It refers to the system and rules that govern a specific language s structure  including its syntax  morphology  and phonology  Using grammatical knowledge helps speakers produce grammatically correct sentences in their language ",
    `#"1.34974e-05"
  },
  {
