  {
    ` "бенуа",
    `!"benoit",
    `#"1.34524e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"бенуа\"`(\"Boulevard\" in `&. This term is typically used in a city context and refers to a broad, straight street or road with a wide pavement (or sidewalk) for pedestrians."
  },
  {
    ` "эй",
    `!"ya, aj, yo, hi",
    `""`$ эй  (pronounced as [aj]) is informal and used to address a single person in a familiar or friendly manner  In formal situations  it s more appropriate to use their name or other titles like Mr   Mrs   etc  Keep in mind that language use and etiquette can vary greatly across different cultures  so it s essential to be respectful and adapt to local norms when interacting with others ",
    `#"1.34503e-05"
  },
  {
    ` "правовых",
    `!"legal",
    `#"1.34503e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"правовых\" is a plural noun that`(\"legal\" or \"related to law\" in `&. It's often used when talking about legal documents, laws, or matters involving the legal system. For example: \"Есть вопросы прававых документов?\" means \"Do you have questions about legal documents?\""
  },
  {
    ` "латинского",
    `!"latin",
