  },
  {
    ` "мексике",
    `!"mexico",
    `#"1.29547e-05",
    `""The Russian word \"Мексике\"`(\"Mexico\" in `&. This is an example of how nouns change in Russian depending on the case they are used in, so it's important to know that \"Мексика\" (without the ending \"-е\") would be the nominative (subject) case form, while \"в Мексике\" means \"in Mexico\" and uses the instrumental case. For learning purposes, it's essential to learn how to correctly conjugate nouns in various cases!"
