    ` "ед",
    `!"mil, plural, conversions, dat",
    `""`$ ед  (pronounced as  ed ) is a verb in the third person singular masculine form  and it means  eats   In Russian  each subject has its own set of forms for verbs  so depending on who or what the subject is  you would use a different form of the verb  For example  if the subject is  я  (I)  you would say  я ем  (I eat)  This specific form   ед   indicates that the subject (he/it) eats  It s essential for `& speakers to understand the concept of declensions when learning Russian  as it can be quite different from `& grammar ",
