    ` "ну",
    `!"say, yeah, guess, just",
    `""`$ ну  (pronounced  nu ) is a versatile and frequently used function word in Russian  It can be roughly translated to `& as  well    then   or  so   Its usage varies greatly depending on context  which makes it a challenging word for `& speakers to master  Here are some common uses:\n\n1  To introduce a topic: ну - Well  let s talk about   \n2  To express agreement or understanding: ну - Yes  I understand  okay \n3  To show surprise or disbelief: ну - Really?\n4  As a filler word: In casual speech  ну can be used as a filler similar to  um  in `& \n5  To suggest an action: ну-pozhalovat sya - Let me introduce myself (lit  Shall I introduce myself?)\n6  As an alternative question marker: ну или   ? - Either    or? (lit  Well  either   )\n7  In a rhetorical question to express disappointment or irony: Ну что же это за жизнь  - What a life  (lit  Well  what kind of life is this?)",
