    `""`$ казачье  (kazach ie) can be translated as  Cossack  or  Cossack-style   In historical context  it refers to a group of semi-autonomous  nomadic people who lived along the rivers in Eastern Europe and Southern Russia  They were known for their military skills  independence  and unique culture  Today  the term is often used to describe things related to or reminiscent of Cossack traditions  such as clothing  music  or architecture ",
