  },
  {
    ` "эдгар",
    `!"edgar",
    `#"1.02966e-05",
    `""The Russian word Эдгар (Edgar) is a proper name and translates directly to `& as Edgar. This name originated in Old `& and means \"wealthy spearman,\" consisting of the elements ead (wealth) and gar (spear). It was popular during the medieval period and throughout history, with notable figures such as Edgar the Peaceful (King of England) and Edgar Allan Poe (American author) bearing this name."
  },
  {
    ` "классе",
    `!"classes",
    `""`$ классе  (transliterated as  klasse ) is not commonly used in modern Russian language  However  if you come across it  it originates from the German word  Klasse  which means a group or class  particularly a school class  In a historical context  it was used to refer to social classes in Russia during the Soviet era  But today  it s not widely used and may cause confusion due to its outdated connotations  Instead  Russians use more common terms such as  класс  (transliterated as  klass ) or  круг  (transliterated as  krug )  meaning class in a school setting or social group  respectively ",
    `#"1.02946e-05"
  },
  {
