    `#"1.01983e-05",
    `""In `&, the Russian word \"давида\" does not have a direct translation as it is a name derived from Hebrew, meaning \"beloved\". However, in Russian, it is pronounced as \"Davida\". If you are learning Russian and encountering names like Davida, remember that they are usually translated by their meanings when used in `& sentences. For example, in the sentence \"Её зовут Давида\" (Her name is Davida), the meaning of Davida remains unchanged, while the gender is indicated by the adjectival ending -a at the end of her name."
  },
  {
    ` "цивилизация",
    `!"civilization",
    `""`$ цивилизация  (civilization) is made up of two words   цивилизованный  (civilized) and  -изация   To understand  цивилизованный   it s important to note that in the Russian context  this term refers not just to adhering to specific cultural norms or manners but also to being educated  enlightened  and progressive  It implies a sense of refinement  understanding of social rules  and having access to knowledge  culture  and technology  This meaning is slightly different from how the word  civilized  is commonly used in `&  where it tends to emphasize cultural development but without necessarily implying sophistication or education ",
