    ` "исландии",
    `!"iceland",
    `#"1.01922e-05",
    `""The Russian word Исландия`(Iceland in `&. When learning Russian, remember that each letter corresponds to a specific sound. In this case, \"И\" (I) sounds like the `& 'ee' as in 'tree', while \"С\" (S) and \"Л\" (L) represent the same letters in both languages, and \"А\" (A) is similar to the vowel in the `& word 'a'. The 'd' sound in Iceland doesn't directly translate but is represented by the \"Д\" (D) letter in Russian words. However, since Исландия starts with \"И\", it is considered a starting consonant and takes the soft form of the letter \"д\". Thus, the pronunciation for Исландия in Russian would be similar to 'is-lahn-dye-ah'."
  },
