    `!"novgorod, riga",
    `#"9.9485e-06",
    `""The Russian word Псков`(Pskov in `&. It is a city located in western Russia and is one of the oldest cities in the country."
  },
  {
    ` "приехал",
    `!"travelled, traveled",
    `""`$ приехал  (priekhal) can be translated to `& as  arrived   This verb is used in the Past Tense form to express that someone or something came or traveled to a specific place  For example  you could say  Я приехал в Москву  ( ya priekhal v Moskva )  which means  I arrived in Moscow  ",
    `#"9.9464e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "традиционный",
    `!"traditional",
    `""`$ традиционный  (traditsionnyj)`( traditional  in `&  It refers to something that is handed down from generation to generation  customary  or characteristic of a particular culture  region  or group  In other words  it signifies a practice or belief that has been long-established and continues to be practiced by a community ",
    `#"9.9464e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "фольклор",
    `!"folklore",
    `""`$ фольклор  (pronounced: fol klor)`( folklore  in `&  It refers to traditional beliefs  legends  stories  customs  and art that are passed down within a culture or group of people by word of mouth or other means outside the formal written tradition  Folklore encompasses various forms such as myths  folktales  ballads  proverbs  songs  riddles  jokes  and local superstitions  In Russian culture  folklore plays an essential role in preserving national identity  history  and values ",
    `#"9.9464e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "марксизма",
    `!"marxism",
    `#"9.9464e-06",
    `""Marxism in `& is \"Markszim\" in Russian. However, it's more common to use a transliteration like \"Markssizm\". The 'sh' in Russian (ш) is pronounced similar to the 's' sound in `& and not like the 'sh' in \"ship\"."
  },
  {
    ` "монгольского",
    `!"mongol, mongolian",
    `#"9.9464e-06",
    `""Mongolian in Russian is \"Монгольский\". If you're learning Russian, try repeating this phrase a few times and break down the words into their constituent parts to remember it easily: \"мон\" (mon) and \"гольский\" (gol'skii). Keep practicing, and you will become more fluent!"
  },
  {
    ` "градусов",
    `!"degrees",
    `""`$ градусов  (pronounced gradusov)`( degrees  in `&  particularly when referring to temperature or angle measurements  In the context of temperature  it is often abbreviated as °C (degrees Celsius)  It s essential to note that this term is not related to the word  grad  which means a small unit of land measurement in Russian and `& alike ",
    `#"9.9444e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "мечты",
    `!"dreams",
    `""`$ мечты  (mechty)`( dreams  in `&  It s a noun that refers to ideas or fantasies about something that one hopes or wishes will happen  often implying they are not realities yet  In other words  dreams are aspirations and goals that may seem unattainable at present but hold significant importance for the individual ",
    `#"9.9444e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "пушек",
    `!"cannons, guns",
    `""`$ пушек  (pronounced  puch-ek ) is a feminine plural noun derived from the root word  пушка  (puskha)  which`( cannon  or  artillery piece  in `&  So   пушек  means  cannons  or  artilleries   It s used when referring to multiple cannons or artillery pieces in a feminine context  such as the cannons of a fortress ",
    `#"9.9444e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "мальчика",
    `!"child, boy",
