    `""The Russian word \"войных\" doesn't exist in its given form as it is a plural noun ending that should be attached to another noun, such as \"войн\" (translated as wars). Therefore, the `& translation for \"войны\" (wars) would still be \"wars\". To make it plural in Russian, you'd say \"войны\" (one of the most common ways to form the plural in Russian is by adding an 'ы' at the end of a masculine noun)."
