    `!"subclass",
    `""`$ подкласс  (podklass)`( subclass  in `&  It is a term used in taxonomy  specifically within hierarchical classification systems  denoting a group of species that are more closely related than those in the same class but less so than those in the same order or family  For example  in the animal kingdom  cats and dogs belong to different families  but both could potentially be part of the same subclass (Mammalia) ",
    `#"9.4877e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "пригласил",
    `!"invited",
