  },
  {
    ` "ис",
    `!"fas, mos",
    `#"9.4713e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"ис\" does not have a direct translation in `& as it is a preposition that can mean \"from\" or \"out of\" depending on the context. For example, \"я вышёл из дома\"`(\"I came out of the house.\" In the phrase \"Я учу русский язык ис книги\" (I'm learning Russian from a book), \"ис\" is used in the sense of \"from.\""
  },
  {
    ` "датский",
    `!"danish",
    `""`$ датский  (datsky) is an adjective that refers to something belonging or relating to Denmark or Danes  In `&  you might say  Danish  instead  For example  if someone bakes a pastry similar to the Danish  they could describe it as датский паscal (datskij paskal - Danish pastry) ",
    `#"9.4672e-06"
