  {
    ` "фонетика",
    `!"phonology",
    `"" Фонетика (fonetika) is a Russian term that`( phonetics  in `&  It refers to the systematic study of the speech sounds and their interactions  characteristics  and properties in any given language  This field focuses on analyzing the physical aspects of sounds  such as their pitch  duration  intensity  and quality  and their organization into phonemes (distinct units of sound that differentiate words within a language)  Phonetics helps in understanding the pronunciation of words  distinguishing between similar sounds  and learning to speak or teach a new language ",
    `#"9.4672e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "планирования",
    `!"planning",
    `#"9.4652e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"планирования\"`(\"planning\" in `&. This term is commonly used when discussing scheduling, organizing or strategizing something. For example, \"Я начинаю планировать свой новый проект\" means \"I am planning my new project.\""
  },
  {
    ` "индо",
    `!"indo",
    `#"9.4632e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"индо\" does not have a standard or common translation in `&, as it is a specific geographical term in Russia. It usually refers to the Indian subcontinent or India itself. In a broader context, if used in a sentence, its meaning would be clear from the context. For example, in the sentence \"Я из индо\" (I am from India), \"индо\"`(\"India.\""
  },
  {
