    `""The Russian word \"Джефферсон\"`(\"Jefferson\" in `&. This is the surname of a famous American president, Thomas Jefferson. However, if you are learning Russian and want to say \"Jefferson\" in Russian, you would use \"Джефферсон\"."
  },
  {
    ` "учёной",
    `!"dissertation, doctoral, doctorate",
    `#"9.4468e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"учёный\"`(\"scholar\" or \"scientist\" in `&. It's often used to describe people who have advanced knowledge and expertise in a specific field of study, such as academics, researchers, or specialists."
  },
  {
    ` "материальной",
    `!"physical, tangible",
    `""`$ материальной  (materiál noj) can be translated to  material  or  materialistic  in `&  It refers to things that are physical and tangible  such as objects or resources  or a focus on those things  particularly in terms of wealth or possessions ",
    `#"9.4447e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "панама",
    `!"panama",
    `""`$ панама  (Panama) is a geographical term that refers to a country in Central America  known for the Panama Canal  It s a transliteration of its Spanish name  but it doesn t have a direct translation into `&  In Russian  it s often pronounced as  Панама  ",
    `#"9.4447e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "юности",
    `!"childhood",
    `""`$ юности  (yunost  or yuność) is the female form of  молодости  (molodost  or molodość)  which means  youth  in `&  It refers to a stage or period of life that is characterized by freshness  inexperience  and vigor  typically associated with young adulthood ",
    `#"9.4447e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "рональд",
    `!"ronald",
    `#"9.4447e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"Рональд\" is translated as \"Ronald\" in `&. For those learning Russian, it's essential to understand that Russian often keeps foreign names intact without translating them. So when you see \"Рональд,\" just remember it's the Russian version of the `& name \"Ronald.\"\n\nIn case you come across a name with a different spelling or pronunciation, remember that it may be essential to learn the correct Cyrillic spelling and pronunciation rules. Good luck with your studies!"
  },
  {
    ` "баланс",
    `!"balance",
