    ` "линч",
    `!"lynch",
    `""`$ линч  (linch) is derived from the `& term  lynch   and it refers to an unlawful  violent punishment inflicted by a mob or group without legal authority  It s important to note that the practice of lynching has deep historical roots in many societies but was especially prevalent in certain regions of the United States during the late 19th and early 20th centuries  The term  lynch  is often used to describe similar acts of mob violence in other countries  including Russia  It s essential to remember that such actions are illegal and morally reprehensible ",
