    `""The Russian word \"старом\" is an adverbial noun in the Genitive singular case, and its direct translation to `& would be \"old\" or \"ancient\", depending on the context. It's essential to note that learning cases and their endings are crucial when translating Russian words accurately. For example, \"старому\" is the genitive plural form, which means \"to the old (ones)\" or \"of the ancient (things)\". Learning these rules will help you understand and use the language more effectively."
