    `""The Russian word Кобург`(Coburg in `&. It's a German city and also a title of nobility in Austria-Hungary and Germany. For learning Russian, it can be helpful to note that \"Коburg\" is spelled with Cyrillic letters as К о б у р г."
  },
  {
    ` "лира",
    `!"argo, sterling, centaur, harp",
    `""`$ лира  (pronounced  lira ) is actually the former name of the currency of Russia  It was used from 1704 until 2010  when it was replaced by the Ruble (Рубль)  However  in modern usage  people often use the term  ruble  to refer to the Russian currency  So  while you might come across the word  lira  in historical texts or contexts about Russia  it s important to know that it is no longer used as the official currency of the country ",
    `#"7.958e-06"
  },
