  },
  {
    ` "поло",
    `!"polo",
    `""`$ поло  (pronounced: polo) is a gender-neutral term that can refer to clothing  specifically shirts or blouses  However  it s important to note that this word changes form depending on its grammatical function in a sentence  For example  in the singular nominative case  it becomes  поло  (masculine)   платье  (feminine) or  полку  (neuter)  In the plural nominative case  it remains as  поло   So when people say  Я ношу поло  ( I wear a shirt/blouse )  it s using the masculine form of the word in the singular nominative case ",
