    ` "непустое",
    `!"mixed",
    `#"7.8924e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"непустое\" can be translated to `& as \"not empty.\" It is an adjective, typically used to describe a container or space that is not vacant. For example: \"Это не пустое место,\" which means \"This place is not empty.\" To someone learning Russian, it's important to note the negative prefix \"не-\" at the beginning of the word indicates negation, so in this case, \"not empty\" refers to something that is filled or occupied."
