  },
  {
    ` "варшаве",
    `!"warsaw",
    `#"7.8085e-06",
    `""In `&, the word \"Варшаве\" is \"Warsaw\". This is a city in Poland, and it's the capital of the country. It's important to note that in Russian, the correct genitive case for Warsaw would be \"Варшаве\", which can translate as \"in Warsaw\" or \"of Warsaw\" when used in sentences. Learning to properly use cases is a crucial part of mastering the Russian language!"
