    `""The Russian word \"супермен\"`(\"Superman\" in `&. If you're learning Russian, you can break down this compound noun into two parts: \"Супер\" which means \"super\" or \"very good\", and \"Мен\" which is short for \"Мужчина\", meaning \"man\". Together they form the name of a popular DC Comics superhero."
  },
  {
    ` "курганская",
    `!"altai, oblast",
    `#"7.6426e-06",
    `""In `&, the Russian word \"курганская\" (kurganskaya) is a feminine adjective derived from the noun \"курган\" (kurgan), meaning 'burial mound' or 'tumulus'. So, \"курганская\" generally refers to something related to a kurgan or originating from a region with kurgans. For example, \"Курганская область\" translates as \"Kurgan Oblast\", which is a region in Western Siberia, Russia."
  },
  {
    ` "выступить",
    `!"participate, join",
    `""`$ выступить  (vyystupit) can be translated to `& as  to speak out    to make a statement   or more generally   to take action   It often implies making a public appearance  giving a speech  or expressing one s opinions or views in a formal or official context  In informal settings  it could also mean  to start  or  to act  ",
