  },
  {
    ` "преобразована",
    `!"renamed",
    `#"7.6385e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"преобразована\"`(\"transformed\" in `&. For someone learning Russian, you can remember that \"преобразована\" is derived from the root words \"преобразовать\" (to transform) and \"-ана\" which is a suffix often used to denote the past participle or passive voice of verbs in Russian. So, \"преобразована\" means something has been transformed."
  },
  {
    ` "материи",
    `!"universe, cosmic",
    `""`$ материи  (matérii) is a plural form of the singular noun  материя  (materiya)  which translates directly to  material  in `&  It refers to any tangible substance or matter used to make or produce something  such as a building material like brick or wood  or an intangible substance like ideas or information ",
