    `#"7.618e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "петром",
    `!"alexei, dmitry, petrus, tsar",
    `#"7.618e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"Петром\" is a patronymic, derived from the male given name \"Пётр\" (Petr). It is traditionally used after a man's given name as a way of indicating one's father's name in Russian-speaking families. So, if someone's full name is Petrom Ivanovich, it means that his given name is Petr and his father's name is Ivan. In `&, the equivalent structure would be using a middle name based on the father's name, such as Peter Johnson Jr. or Peter Johnson son of John."
  },
  {
    ` "маленьких",
    `!"small, tiny",
    `""`$ маленьких  (malyen kih) is a plural form of the adjective  маленький  (malyen kij)  which means  small  or  little   So   маленьких  refers to multiple small or little things ",
    `#"7.616e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "отдых",
    `!"vacation",
