  },
  {
    ` "таксон",
    `!"taxon",
    `""`$ таксон  (pronounced: takson) is derived from the Greek word  τάξις  (taxis)  which means order or arrangement  In Russian  the term  таксон  is most commonly used in the field of biology and refers to a taxon  or a group of organisms that are closely related by evolution and share common characteristics  It can be further broken down into subcategories such as phylum  class  order  family  genus  and species  In this context   таксон  helps systematically classify different species based on their shared traits ",
