  },
  {
    ` "лезги",
    `!"honoured, honored, honorary",
    `""`$ лезги  (Lezhy) is an ethnonym  referring to a group of people who predominantly inhabit the North Caucasus region  specifically in Dagestan and adjacent areas  They are often known as the Lezgians or Lezghis in `&  This term can also refer to their language  which belongs to the Lezgian branch of the Northeastern Caucasian (or Nakh-Daghestanian) family  It s essential to note that using ethnic terms should be done with respect and sensitivity  acknowledging the cultural diversity and rich history of these groups ",
