  {
    ` "неверным",
    `!"incorrect",
    `""`$ неверным  (pronounced ne-ver -nym)`( unfaithful  in `&  It is usually used to refer to a person who is unfaithful or disloyal in a relationship  or to something that does not function as it should and is therefore unreliable ",
    `#"6.8685e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "оценить",
    `!"assess, evaluate",
    `""`$ оценить  (o-tsenit ) can be translated to `& as  to estimate    to appraise   or  to assess   It means to form a judgment about something based on analysis  experience  or information  For example  if you want to say  I will estimate the cost of this project  in Russian  you would say  Я оценюю стоимость этого проекта  (Ya otsenyu stoimost  etogo proekta) ",
    `#"6.8685e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "признаку",
    `!"discriminate, grouping, ethnicity, groupings",
    `""`$ признаку  (priznaku) can be translated to `& as  symptom   but more specifically  it refers to a sign or indication of something  especially when used in a medical context  It s derived from the verb  признавать  (priznavat)  which means  to acknowledge  or  admit  ",
    `#"6.8685e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "проживал",
    `!"lived",
    `""`$ проживал  (pronounced as  pro-zhi-vahl ) is a past tense of the verb  жить  (to live)  more specifically  it means  used to live in  or  previously resided in   For example:  Я проживал в Москве `( I used to live in Moscow  or  I previously resided in Moscow  ",
    `#"6.8685e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "огпу",
    `!"nkvd",
    `#"6.8685e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"ОГПУ\" stands for \"Объединённое господарственное политическое управление,\" which`(\"Unified State Political Administration\" in `&. It was a Soviet state security agency that existed from 1922 until 1934, when it was split into the NKVD (People's Commissariat of Internal Affairs) and the Red Army's military counterintelligence division (the GPU within the Red Army became the Military Counterintelligence Directorate). The OGPU was responsible for maintaining order and enforcing political policies in the Soviet Union."
  },
  {
    ` "реставрация",
    `!"restoration",
    `"" Реставрация (restauratsiya) in Russian refers to restoration or renovation  It is commonly used to denote the process of restoring a building  work of art  or other cultural heritage item to its original condition after decay  damage  or destruction  This could involve repairing damaged areas  cleaning  and sometimes recreating lost elements based on historical evidence ",
    `#"6.8665e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "точных",
    `!"precise, accurate",
