    `#"6.8665e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "орехово",
    `!"smolensk, voronezh, krasnodar, oblast",
    `#"6.8665e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"орехово\"`(\"almond\" in `&. This word is often used when referring to almond-flavored or almond-based foods and products. Learning basic vocabulary like this can help you navigate conversations, food labels, and recipes more easily as you continue your journey to learn Russian!"
  },
  {
    ` "эли",
    `!"haim, gabriel, kaplan, marcel",
    `""`$ эли  (pronounced as  e-li ) is a diminutive form of the name Helena  In some contexts  it can also be used as a shortened version of the surname Saveliev or Savelyev  which are derived from the male name Savely (a Russian variant of Clement)  It s important to note that using diminutives in Russia is a common way to express affection  familiarity  or informality ",
    `#"6.8644e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "профессоров",
    `!"professors",
    `#"6.8644e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"профессор\"`(\"professor\" in `&. This term is used to refer to a person who holds the rank of professor at a university or college, typically holding a Ph.D. degree and specializing in teaching and researching within their field of expertise."
  },
  {
    ` "компартии",
    `!"communist",
    `#"6.8644e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"компартии\"`(\"Communist Party\" in `&. It's a compound noun where \"ком-\" stands for \"Коммунистический\" (Communist) and \"-партия\" is short for \"Партия\" (Party). When learning Russian, it can be helpful to break down unfamiliar words into their constituent parts, so you understand the meaning more easily."
  },
  {
    ` "аналогичный",
    `!"similar",
    `""`$ аналогичный  (analogichnyj) can be translated to `& as  analogous  or  similar in some respects   It is often used to compare things that have certain characteristics  but are not identical  For example  if someone says that a cat and a dog are аналогичные (analogichnyje)  it means they are similar because they are both pets and mammals  even though they are different species ",
    `#"6.8624e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "писателях",
    `!"writers",
    `""`$ писателях  (pishateliakh) is the plural form of  писатель  (pisatel )  which translates directly to  writer  in `&  So   писателях  refers to a group or multiple writers in context ",
    `#"6.8624e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "спроса",
    `!"prices, demand, market",
    `"" Спроса (sprosha) is a Russian noun that`( demand  or  request  in `&  It is commonly used in business  economics  and everyday conversations to discuss needs  wants  or orders for goods or services ",
    `#"6.8624e-06"
  },
  {
    ` "чукотский",
    `!"alaskan, siberian",
    `""Чукотский (Chukotsky) is a language spoken by the Chukchi people  one of the indigenous groups in the Far East of Russia  It belongs to the Chukot-Kamchatka branch of the Paleo-Siberian languages  This language has its own unique phonetic and grammatical structure  distinct from the more widely spoken Russian language ",
