    ` "анастасий",
    `!"patriarch, ignatius, theodosius, antioch",
    `#"6.6617e-06",
    `""The Russian word \"Анастасий\"`(\"Anastasius\" in `&. If you are learning Russian and would like more information or examples on how to use this name, I can help with that as well! For example:\n\n* Анастасия - feminine form of the name, which`(Anastasia in `&.\n* Анастасий Иванович - full name of a male, meaning Anastasius Ivanovich. In Russian culture, a patronymic is typically added after the given name and denotes the father's first name (in this case, Иван, or Ivan).\n* Это имя пришло из византийской империи - This name comes from the Byzantine Empire refers to the history of the name."
  },
