    ` "падеж",
    `!"verb, noun",
    `"" The Russian term  падеж  (padezh) is equivalent to the `& term  case   both in grammar  In Russian grammar  cases are a set of inflections that denote the relationship between words within a sentence - subject  object  location  etc  Unlike `&  which only has two cases (subjective and objective)  Russian has six: nominative  genitive  dative  accusative  instrumental  and prepositional  Each case is marked by specific endings on nouns and pronouns  allowing for greater flexibility and precision in sentence construction ",
