    ` "ь",
    `!"pronounced, spelling, ch",
    `""ь (hard sign  also known as  soft sign ) in Russian is a diacritical mark used in the Cyrillic script  It doesn t represent any sound by itself but changes the pronunciation of the following consonant letter it precedes  Generally  it softens the hard consonants (к  т  п  с  ш  ж  з  ч  х) to their corresponding soft counterparts (къ  ц  тс  сх  шч  жж  зж  чь  хь)  which are similar to the `&  y  sound as in  yes   However  this rule doesn t apply consistently across all words and it s essential to learn them through proper pronunciation guides or lessons ",
