    ` "таймс",
    `!"york, street, manhattan, newsweek",
    `""`$ таймс  (pronounced [tɐɪ ms]) is a transliteration of the `& word  times   In Russian  it can refer to multiple things:\n\n1  Chronological time  as in  What time is it?  (in this context  the correct translation would be  Время?  or  Час?   depending on the level of formality)\n2  Newspaper or magazine titles that are named  Times   such as The Times (a major British daily newspaper)  In these cases  the correct Russian transliteration would be  Таймс   However  it is more common to translate a newspaper title directly into Russian  so you might see something like  Лондонские Вести  for  The Times  of London \n3  A specific genre of song or musical composition known as a  time  (время)  where the focus is on the rhythmic patterns rather than melody or harmony  In this context  the word  таймс  would not be used since it s a transliteration of an `& term and doesn t have this meaning in Russian \n\nIt s essential to consider the context when using or interpreting ",
