    ` "невисокосный",
    `!"public, speeches",
    `""`$ невисокосный  (nevysokosny) is an adjective and its direct translation to `& would be  not leap year   It s used to refer to years that are not a leap year  in contrast to високосный (vysokosny)  which means  leap year   Leap years are years with 366 days instead of the usual 365  In the Gregorian calendar  leap years occur every four years  if the year can be exactly divided by four; however  years that are multiples of 100 are not leap years  unless they are also multiples of 400  which is a leap year  This rule is followed to keep the calendar accurate with the Earth s revolutions around the Sun ",
